    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's helpful. One thing though—some critics argue that the money often goes to corrupt regimes or doesn't even reach the people who need it, which makes the 'strategic investment' argument look a bit hollow. Given that, how do we address the idea that foreign aid is fundamentally broken or even counterproductive? I want to show that the opposition's arguments are essentially misguided and that the only real solution is to double down on our commitment rather than cutting it.",
