      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The criticism of corruption is a failure of implementation, not a failure of the principle of aid itself. Instead of abandoning the mission, we must demand greater transparency and partner with vetted, effective local organizations. Cutting aid based on the actions of a few corrupt actors is equivalent to abandoning the sick because some doctors are incompetent. Our commitment must be unwavering, but our oversight must be absolute.",
      "source": "target",
